# ============================================================================
# PULSE — API environment
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# Nothing in this file is read by the browser bundle. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed `VITE_`, and none of these are — the publishable Razorpay
# key reaches the page from `POST /api/subscription/checkout` at runtime, so
# rotating keys never needs a frontend rebuild.
# ============================================================================

# --- Razorpay -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Account & Settings → API Keys. A test key looks like `rzp_test_…`;
# the server reports which mode it is in on startup and at GET /api/health.
PAYMENT_KEY_ID=rzp_test_replace_me
PAYMENT_KEY_SECRET=replace_me

# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks. The secret you typed when creating the
# webhook, not the API key secret. Without it, deliveries are rejected rather
# than trusted — see server/routes/webhooks.ts.
WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace_me

# Created by `npm run razorpay:setup`, which reads the amounts from
# shared/plans.ts so Razorpay cannot disagree with the pricing page.
RAZORPAY_PLAN_INDIVIDUAL=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_FAMILY=

# --- Sessions -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs the session cookie. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Changing it invalidates every existing session.
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Server -------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=4000
# SQLite file. Created on first boot along with its parent directory.
DATABASE_URL=./data/pulse.sqlite

# --- Cross-origin -------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when the frontend is served from a different origin than the API.
# In development the Vite proxy makes them the same origin, so leave these
# alone. If you do split origins, `none` also requires COOKIE_SECURE=true.
# APP_ORIGIN=https://pulse.example.com
# COOKIE_SAMESITE=lax
# COOKIE_SECURE=true
